51-00813-0100-4001, p. 77), for the Rosemount 3051CFC_C Compact Orifice Flow Meter with Conditioning Option C, ranges 2–3, a beta ratio of 0.50 gives an accuracy of ±1.95% of flow rate at 8:1 flow turndown.\", \"not_present\": false}"}}}
{"qid": "b02", "family": "b", "split": "dev", "method": "M3", "model": "glm", "answer": {"method": "M3", "model": "glm", "final": {"answer": "GV-14-2 is a globe valve in the P&ID, and its datasheet is the GF Piping Systems Type 165 2/2-way solenoid valve datasheet. That datasheet does give Kv values, but they depend on the valve's nominal size, which is not stated for GV-14-2 in the P&ID or the excerpts: Kv is 83 l/min for DN15, 100 l/min for DN20, 233 l/min for DN25, 267 l/min for DN32, 500 l/min for DN40, and 600 l/min for DN50 (measured with water at +20 °C, 1 bar pressure at the valve inlet and free outlet). The datasheet also notes a minimum differential pressure of 0.5 bar is required to open and close the valve. The exact flow GV-14-2 passes when fully open therefore cannot be determined from the documents, since its size is not given.", "not_present": false}, "outcome": "ANSWERED", "route": ["context_rag+chunks"], "cypher": [], "sources": [{"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "pages": [36, 32, 23]}, {"document_id": "gfps-165-solenoid-valve", "pages": [5, 2, 1, 3]}, {"document_id": "flowserve-worcester-f51-f52", "pages": [10]}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "pages": [106, 98, 34, 32]}], "latency_s": 11.847047899966128, "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 53853, "completion_tokens": 1645, "cost_usd": 0.0009394261, "spent_usd": 0.0009391261, "n_calls": 2, "n_cached": 1, "models": ["qwen/qwen3-embedding-8b", "z-ai/glm-5.3-flash"]}, "trace": {"chunks": [{"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 36, "score": 0.6223}, {"document_id": "gfps-165-solenoid-valve", "page": 5, "score": 0.611}, {"document_id": "gfps-165-solenoid-valve", "page": 2, "score": 0.6091}, {"document_id": "flowserve-worcester-f51-f52", "page": 10, "score": 0.5881}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 106, "score": 0.5733}, {"document_id": "gfps-165-solenoid-valve", "page": 1, "score": 0.573}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 32, "score": 0.5729}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 23, "score": 0.5704}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 98, "score": 0.5692}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 34, "score": 0.5667}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 32, "score": 0.5583}, {"document_id": "gfps-165-solenoid-valve", "page": 3, "score": 0.558}], "prompt_chars": 132529, "reply": "{\"answer\": \"GV-14-2 is a globe valve in the P&ID, and its datasheet is the GF Piping Systems Type 165 2/2-way solenoid valve datasheet. That datasheet does give Kv values, but they depend on the valve's nominal size, which is not stated for GV-14-2 in the P&ID or the excerpts: Kv is 83 l/min for DN15, 100 l/min for DN20, 233 l/min for DN25, 267 l/min for DN32, 500 l/min for DN40, and 600 l/min for DN50 (measured with water at +20 °C, 1 bar pressure at the valve inlet and free outlet). The datasheet also notes a minimum differential pressure of 0.5 bar is required to open and close the valve. The exact flow GV-14-2 passes when fully open therefore cannot be determined from the documents, since its size is not given.\", \"not_present\": false}"}}}
{"qid": "b03", "family": "b", "split": "dev", "method": "M3", "model": "glm", "answer": {"method": "M3", "model": "glm", "final": {"answer": "GV-1-1 is covered by the GF Piping Systems Type 165 2/2-way solenoid valve datasheet, which lists the nominal mode of operation as 'Continuous operation 100 % ED'. So the valve can be energized continuously for a full shift; the datasheet does not state any duty-cycle restriction or coil-overheating limitation.", "not_present": false}, "outcome": "ANSWERED", "route": ["context_rag+chunks"], "cypher": [], "sources": [{"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "pages": [36, 18]}, {"document_id": "gfps-165-solenoid-valve", "pages": [6, 2, 1, 3, 4]}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "pages": [16, 93, 47, 114, 36]}], "latency_s": 9.562433899962343, "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 52602, "completion_tokens": 1342, "cost_usd": 0.0009090226, "spent_usd": 0.0009087326, "n_calls": 2, "n_cached": 1, "models": ["qwen/qwen3-embedding-8b", "z-ai/glm-5.3-flash"]}, "trace": {"chunks": [{"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 36, "score": 0.6704}, {"document_id": "gfps-165-solenoid-valve", "page": 6, "score": 0.5951}, {"document_id": "gfps-165-solenoid-valve", "page": 2, "score": 0.5944}, {"document_id": "gfps-165-solenoid-valve", "page": 1, "score": 0.5928}, {"document_id": "gfps-165-solenoid-valve", "page": 3, "score": 0.5879}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 16, "score": 0.5661}, {"document_id": "gfps-165-solenoid-valve", "page": 4, "score": 0.5623}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 18, "score": 0.5623}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 93, "score": 0.5619}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 47, "score": 0.5569}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 114, "score": 0.5564}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 36, "score": 0.5515}], "prompt_chars": 131815, "reply": "{\"answer\": \"GV-1-1 is covered by the GF Piping Systems Type 165 2/2-way solenoid valve datasheet, which lists the nominal mode of operation as 'Continuous operation 100 % ED'. So the valve can be energized continuously for a full shift; the datasheet does not state any duty-cycle restriction or coil-overheating limitation.\", \"not_present\": false}"}}}
{"qid": "b04", "family": "b", "split": "dev", "method": "M3", "model": "glm", "answer": {"method": "M3", "model": "glm", "final": {"answer": "GV-11-2 is drawn as a globe (solenoid) valve, and the GF Piping Systems Type 165 2/2-way solenoid valve datasheet that covers the GV tags shows it is an electrically operated solenoid valve, so it does need power. The datasheet lists supply voltage options of 24V DC, 230V 50/60Hz AC, and 115V 50/60Hz AC (voltage tolerance ±10%), with separate ordering codes for each voltage. 24V DC is therefore a supported option and would work if the valve is the 24V DC variant; the documents do not state which voltage variant GV-11-2 itself is equipped with.", "not_present": false}, "outcome": "ANSWERED", "route": ["context_rag+chunks"], "cypher": [], "sources": [{"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "pages": [36]}, {"document_id": "gfps-165-solenoid-valve", "pages": [6, 2, 4, 5, 1, 3]}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "pages": [87, 32, 47, 16, 98]}], "latency_s": 2.9058110000332817, "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 52863, "completion_tokens": 371, "cost_usd": 0.00810865, "spent_usd": 0.0081082, "n_calls": 2, "n_cached": 1, "models": ["qwen/qwen3-embedding-8b", "z-ai/glm-5.3-flash"]}, "trace": {"chunks": [{"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 36, "score": 0.6186}, {"document_id": "gfps-165-solenoid-valve", "page": 6, "score": 0.6082}, {"document_id": "gfps-165-solenoid-valve", "page": 2, "score": 0.5798}, {"document_id": "gfps-165-solenoid-valve", "page": 4, "score": 0.5752}, {"document_id": "gfps-165-solenoid-valve", "page": 5, "score": 0.567}, {"document_id": "gfps-165-solenoid-valve", "page": 1, "score": 0.5594}, {"document_id": "gfps-165-solenoid-valve", "page": 3, "score": 0.5559}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 87, "score": 0.5526}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 32, "score": 0.5485}, {"document_id": "rosemount-3051-00813-0100-4001", "page": 47, "score": 0.