{"qid": "c03", "family": "c", "split": "dev", "method": "M3", "model": "glm", "answer": {"method": "M3", "model": "glm", "final": {"answer": "The valve operated by loop FIC-14-1 is FV-14-1, which per the datasheet mapping is a Fisher ET/EAT/ETR sliding-stem control valve (fisher-et-d100022x012). The bulletin lists these trim options: standard trims 1, 4, 27, 29, 37 and 37H (Figure 13), Cavitrol III one-stage and two-stage cages (trim 76, Figure 14), NACE/sour-service trims 85, 86 and 87 (Figure 15), plus Whisper Trim III, Whisper NXG Trim and WhisperFlo cages. For high pressure drop (cavitation damage), the Cavitrol III cages are offered — a standard-travel one-stage cage and a long-travel two-stage cage are available in NPS 1 through NPS 8 ET valves. For noise, the Whisper Trim III, Whisper NXG Trim and WhisperFlo cages attenuate aerodynamic noise in gaseous service. The datasheet excerpts do not state which specific trim is actually fitted on FV-14-1.", "not_present": false}, "outcome": "ANSWERED", "route": ["context_rag+chunks"], "cypher": [], "sources": [{"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "pages": [18, 3, 6, 9, 26, 7, 32, 1, 25, 2, 36, 19]}], "latency_s": 25.315202600031625, "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 55247, "completion_tokens": 3737, "cost_usd": 0.0010355608, "spent_usd": 0.0010352308, "n_calls": 2, "n_cached": 1, "models": ["qwen/qwen3-embedding-8b", "z-ai/glm-5.3-flash"]}, "trace": {"chunks": [{"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 18, "score": 0.6559}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 3, "score": 0.6154}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 6, "score": 0.6149}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 9, "score": 0.6066}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 26, "score": 0.6051}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 7, "score": 0.6021}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 32, "score": 0.5964}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 1, "score": 0.5942}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 25, "score": 0.5858}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 2, "score": 0.5854}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 36, "score": 0.5831}, {"document_id": "fisher-et-d100022x012", "page": 19, "score": 0.583}], "prompt_chars": 139484, "reply": "{\"answer\": \"The valve operated by loop FIC-14-1 is FV-14-1, which per the datasheet mapping is a Fisher ET/EAT/ETR sliding-stem control valve (fisher-et-d100022x012). The bulletin lists these trim options: standard trims 1, 4, 27, 29, 37 and 37H (Figure 13), Cavitrol III one-stage and two-stage cages (trim 76, Figure 14), NACE/sour-service trims 85, 86 and 87 (Figure 15), plus Whisper Trim III, Whisper NXG Trim and WhisperFlo cages. For high pressure drop (cavitation damage), the Cavitrol III cages are offered — a standard-travel one-stage cage and a long-travel two-stage cage are available in NPS 1 through NPS 8 ET valves. For noise, the Whisper Trim III, Whisper NXG Trim and WhisperFlo cages attenuate aerodynamic noise in gaseous service. The datasheet excerpts do not state which specific trim is actually fitted on FV-14-1.\", \"not_present\": false}"}}}
