08}], "prompt_chars": 138554, "reply": "{\"answer\": \"A Fisher ET is a single-port, globe-style control valve with cage guiding, a balanced valve plug, and push-down-to-close valve plug action (per the Fisher ET/EAT/ETR product bulletin D100022X012). Yes, it is the valve body style — the ET designation refers to the valve body/product, of which the EAT is the angle version and the ETR the push-down-to-open version. However, the provided P&ID excerpt contains only nodes and no piping edges, so the documents do not state which item is directly upstream of BV-12-1; that part of the question is not stated.\", \"not_present\": false}"}}}
